{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/424925-necropoli-of-the-world-cities-town-and-outposts","id":424925,"title":"Necropoli of the World: Cities, town, and outposts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-01T23:54:01-08:00","id":424925,"title":"Necropoli of the World: Cities, town, and outposts","content":"This is from Whither's idea. Help flesh out the Shadowlands with your area's Cities of the Dead.<br /> <br /> Springfield, Missouri - The Mangled Citadel<br /> The center of Southwest Missouri, the Necropolis of Springfield. It's a miss-mash of various Haunts and destruction. The materials used for it's buildings ranging from the Civil War to the 1960s. There are a few &quot;bleed through&quot; Haunts scattered through out the city. Pythian Castle is the most famous and one most Wraiths tend to avoid with it's German POWs, orphans, and one perverted Specter. Lincoln Hall of Ozarks Technical Community and a few locations at Drury College are the hardest ones to pierce through and gain access to the Skinlands. Other locations like the Landers Theater are about the average range. The Citadel at the center of Springfield is the only building in the entire Necropolis that is the most consistent. With all the construction and deconstruction of Springfield, whole Haunts are a rarity. The outskirts of the Necropolis is shanty town. Materials from the deconstruction cross over in splinters, scrap heaps, and if your luck, complete walls. The closer you get to the Citadel, the buildings that still stand are a menagerie of the major time periods Springfield went through. The Civil War, Roaring 20s, and the 50s. You can easily tell which look is which. Springfield is practically a capital in of itself, with smaller Necropoli like Bolivar, Morrisville, Joplin, Lebanon, Branson, and others the region almost operates like a small country with each small Necropoli providing trade and even defense. And small cemeteries, still functioning and abandoned, serving as outposts for any Wraith that might be trapped in a Maelstrom. There is one area that is an oddity, Wilson's Creek. Those who venture there will witness a repeating battle from the Civil War. It goes over the course of three days, and keeps looping for those three days. The only Wraiths that are sentient reside in the farmhouse overlooking the battlefield. While the Relics are reclaimed by the battlefield every third day, it's treated like a mine since the Corpus harvested from the battlefield never returns to its owner. For the owners are tied to the land and the land provides new Corpus to the echos. Those who like to risk &quot;gold digging&quot;, they would best time their expedition to the battlefield in coordination of the battle itself. The ammunition are Relics and send you to Oblivion.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T19:03:19-07:00","id":435074,"title":"","content":"Well, I was posting to this thread. But like usual by the time I get it written it secretly logs me out. Then it won't let me in to the thread. Then it won't let me post once I claw my way back in. Then everything is gone once I finally find something. So, where ever the rest of the stuff is I am responding to I don't have any clue. But here is the response:<br /> <br /> Part of why I have been writing up my own Wraith game (Wraith Unremitting) is because the classic games were all based on the same lore but had horrible mechanics for interacting. Wraith was the absolute worst of the lot for cross-over. I like NWoD mechanics but CWoD lore. However, my intention is for the real power in KC to be William Rockhill Nelson, a renegade Syndicate mage - beneficent tyrant and patron of the people, who used his craft in Spirit to take control of the Emerald Legion and rule KC Necropolis. Through Pentex the Syndicate rules KC from their offices at 12th and Cherry, but through Necropolis Nelson unravels their schemes, undermines their production, and greases their ever increasingly unsteady grip.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T09:58:56-07:00","id":435856,"title":"","content":"How is Nelson a victim of happenstance? I don't remember how he died (despite being related to the man somewhat distantly...)<br /> <br /> If you are including Nelson, what about Boss Pendergast? As far as actual power in life goes, how can you do better than the man who made his office boy President of the United States?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T13:06:24-07:00","id":437423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whithers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/424925-necropoli-of-the-world-cities-town-and-outposts?p=435074#post435074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I was posting to this thread. But like usual by the time I get it written it secretly logs me out. Then it won't let me in to the thread. Then it won't let me post once I claw my way back in. Then everything is gone once I finally find something. So, where ever the rest of the stuff is I am responding to I don't have any clue. But here is the response:</div> </div> </div> </div>Copy and paste is a life saver when what happens.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T19:43:20-07:00","id":448666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/424925-necropoli-of-the-world-cities-town-and-outposts?p=435856#post435856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is Nelson a victim of happenstance? I don't remember how he died (despite being related to the man somewhat distantly...)<br /> <br /> If you are including Nelson, what about Boss Pendergast? As far as actual power in life goes, how can you do better than the man who made his office boy President of the United States?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a victim of happenstance, of the Syndicate - he was a populist after Trevain. KC was called the City of Philanthropy, but nearly all its early millionaires died penniless around 1900. Truman was friends with Pendergast yes, and Pendergast's father laid the ground work as a city boss for him to take over once he was old enough. But Pendergast wasn't a mage. He was a man with good intentions who used his connections and his prominence to feed his own addictions. Had he not been caught by the Fed.s and sent to prison there is no telling just how far the Baali friends he had just started hooking up with might have gotten with their plans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T10:01:19-07:00","id":449433,"title":"","content":"Hmmm.... it's hard to not feel weird about all that, since some of those people are relatives close enough in generation that my parents knew them. <br /> <br /> Pendergast was the boss of the political party andcontrolled KC politics for decades, was THE major player in Democrat state politics and someone that mattered in national politics. Truman wasn't a buddy, he was effectively as much an employee as modern politicians are of their billionaire backers. That line about making his &quot;office boy president&quot; is a 2nd hand quote. I heard it from someone who was there when he said it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T14:09:13-07:00","id":449757,"title":"","content":"There is a general belief by those backing politicos that they are getting more for their investment than is realistic, and by the politicos that they are getting what is needed to get elected from people that they generally agree with on basics enough not to piss off too much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T18:49:05-07:00","id":450009,"title":"","content":"Santiago de Chile during the 70s and 80s","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T14:42:22-07:00","id":462683,"title":"","content":"Bring out your dead!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T23:35:19-07:00","id":463165,"title":"","content":"I was talking to a player about Wraith, and then he mentioned One place....And i really really, Really...want Rich to explore this site on the Wraith mythos if he hasnt already...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aokigahara\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Aokigahara_and_Misaka_Mountains.JPG/1280px-Aokigahara_and_Misaka_Mountains.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aokigahara\" target=\"_blank\"> Aokigahara - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aokigahara\" target=\"_blank\"> http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aokigahara </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Id imagine it, a Spectre hive. one of the Bigest in the world. The Sea of Crying Trees, The Snake Ropes, The Whispering winds of sorrow, all vegetation corrupted and consumed with the dry blood and rotting flesh, a place made of broken hearts and no hope at all. A place of personal Redemption (?) and yet Failure...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T13:50:16-07:00","id":463843,"title":"","content":"It's a location of concentrated despair, but I'd imagine there are a lot of places in Africa and Asia where atrocities are generating more mortwights and fast-turning spectres. After all, more people jump off the Golden Gate Bridge every year than kill themselves in that forest, and I doubt the former is a massive spectre hive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T19:07:57-07:00","id":464159,"title":"","content":"Only because of the geodesic technocracy dome hidden underneath which captures the dead still attempting to break out of their cauls and then sublimates them into the dark web for shunting tass into primium batteries for Void Engineers to use in their new transsubstantial metaphasic weaponry for defense while remapping the dimension some superstitionists once called the Shadowlands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T03:51:09-07:00","id":465903,"title":"","content":"Manchester, England would be a great place. Its history stretches back at least to Roman times, and it was part of the seat of the House of Lancaster, so would've seen battle during the War of the Roses, when the House of York battled the House of Lancaster for the crown.<br /> <br /> Once called Cottonopolis for its place in the industrial revolution, the Necropolis would be full of ghostly factories, the brutal spinning machines which maimed and killed children, and the slaves brought into nearby Liverpool's docks (and whose backs and blood fed much of the industrial revolution, as well as the city's cotton trade). The city was one of the prime inspirations for Dickens' Hard Times.<br /> <br /> There was the Peterloo Massacre, where hundreds of protesters were killed in the ongoing fight for freedom; the many struggles of the Suffragettes (including Emmeline Pankhurst and her family); the emergence and death of great scientists like Alan Turing (who was basically driven to suicide by the state, and whose memorial statue draws visitors all year round); the deathplace of Oscar Wilde (in the bed of one of his fans); the deathplace of local legend and boxer-cum-drag queen Foo Foo Lammar. <br /> <br /> I imagine Turing's early computers might be relics used by the local Artificers. Imagine if those computers that survived were Inhabited? There's at least one that can write love letters, if I remember correctly.<br /> <br /> In more recent years, 50 men have been dragged, dead, from the canal that runs through the city and along the city's Gay Village (which generates memoriam through its immortalisation in Queer as Folk)--that's in the last five years alone. The canal runs with blood. I imagine in places it becomes a byway into the Tempest and that reapers drag wraiths from the waters every month while still in their cauls.<br /> <br /> The Transgender Memorial probably serves as a huge source of memoriam and pathos for the victims of violence and despair. The nearby HIV Memorial would do the same for sickness. Both statues are overlooked in Sackville Gardens by the bronze statue of Alan Turing, who holds a poisoned apple in his hand (anecdote says this is the origin of the Apple logo, as Turing apparently killed himself with a bite of a poisoned apple--although Apple bosses have said the connection is coincidental).<br /> <br /> The city's Ancoats area has plenty of warehouses and mills which would provide haunts for wraiths.<br /> <br /> As the most diverse city in the UK (with more actual ethnicities than London, even if they compose a smaller percentage of the overall population), there are over 251 languages spoken in the city. There would be wraiths from South Asia along the Curry Mile. Wraiths from Southeast Asia in Chinatown. Plenty of Heretics congregating in the new African churches which are flourishing (which have colourful names like Mountain of Fire and Miracles Ministry).<br /> <br /> The Albert Kennedy Trust was founded when a youth of the same name (who'd been made homeless when he came out as gay) jumped off the top of a city centre carpark. His name still carries a very strong mark of respect.<br /> <br /> Then there's the ghostly legacy of Madchester: wraiths from the Hacienda days of 24 Hour Party People. Wraiths whose lives were filled with ecstasy and house music. Their illegal raves would have created some interesting haunts. The DJs might wield their own unique Keening powers that mimic the effects of coming up on MDMA.<br /> <br /> The legacy of Morrissey and The Smiths (and Oasis and a raft of other bands) would have made a mark too. Manchester's rainy climate and often miserable music lends itself to certain kinds of pathos. Morrissey lovers come to the city from all over the world to complete pilgrimages to him, and visit key locations from his youth.<br /> <br /> The IRA also famously decimated the Arndale Centre (a tatty looking mall), and it was reborn even bigger and better. The remnants would be across the Shroud. Likewise, the Luftwaffe destroyed much during WWII. The local council has also torn down lots of slum housing as gentrification has taken hold--such as the infamous Bullrings in Hulme, which were crumbling towerblocks, allegedly rife with crime.<br /> <br /> Finally, the city-wide riots of a few years ago (sparked by the familiar murder of a black youth by police, and reflected in similar riots across the country) damaged lots of buildings, which would've created new relics and new buildings across the Shroud.<br /> <br /> There's so much there to go on, that I feel compelled to start a wraith game here now!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 04-02-2015, 06:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T12:46:00-07:00","id":466382,"title":"","content":"Two great locations. The Golden Gate Bridge I would label as a bleed through Haunt since it serves kinda like a gateway for Wraiths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}